add(321442,'parked_no_counterexample','primary rooted-tree definitions, conjecture and neighbouring proofs read; multiple exact bounded searches','A topology assignment may depend on the partition. A grove requires either no cross triple or some informative compatible rooted-tree assignment for EVERY nontrivial partition. Strictly informative requires the latter for every such partition. Intersection is as collections of taxon sets.','Enumerated all rooted binary supertrees on 4,5,6 taxa and projected them to input taxon sets. Compatible assignments are restriction-signature classes. A cross triple is resolved iff its rooted resolution is constant in such a class. Exhaustive family classifications and union tests are in logs/groves.log. Mixed 3/4-element taxon sets on six taxa gave 1100 strictly informative families of size 2..4 after a necessary private-taxon filter; 5000 sampled intersecting pairs passed. Seven-taxon bitset computation used all 10395 rooted binary trees, classified 3000 sampled private-taxon families, found 1277 distinct strict families and tested 1000 intersecting pairs without a witness. Full six-taxon all-pairs extension hit the wall cap and is NOT credited as complete.','No general union lemma or counterexample. Need control of resolved triples when a partition of the union masks cross triples of either constituent. Small family tests cannot supply that bridge. The source Remark 3.19 example itself fails the stated strict criterion in our diagnostic; it is an adjacent source defect, not a solution of Conjecture 3.13.','1104.2562, Definitions 2.3-2.4, 3.10, Propositions 3.11-3.12, Conjecture 3.13, Remark 3.19',('logs/groves.log','logs/groves-deep.log','logs/groves-allpairs.log','logs/groves7.log'))
