add(326960,'parked_material_source_definition_gap','literal statement compared with latest supplied primary PDF and original v1','Restricted c_G(H) is defined in the source. The source defines an s-trap as a VERTEX whose neighbours are covered by closed cop neighbourhoods using floor(s) cops outside that vertex; it does not define H being an s-trap.','Read Lemma 2 and the restricted-movement induction. Read the vertex trap definition and Conjecture 8 about teleporting cops. Also fetched and read v1; it does not repair the database subgraph-trap definition. No invented subgraph predicate was searched.','Exact source definition and quantifiers for the advertised subgraph trap condition are missing. A graph search under a guessed definition would not test the literal endpoint. Park rather than widen to teleporting-cop equality.','1312.7555, Lemma 2, Section 3 vertex traps, Conjecture 8; original v1',extra=('sources/1312.7555v1.pdf.receipt.json',))
add(327368,'parked_bounded_nonfinding_source_boundary','primary definitions, Theorem 3.1 proof, Conjecture 3.2 and Appendix A code read; two algorithms used','nu(f) is the number of adjacent bit changes (one less than the number of constant blocks), not an isometric-embedding index. Source experimental range is 3 <= |f| < d.','Early exact NetworkX isomorphism search completed dimensions 4..7; dimension 8 onward hit CPU cap. Replaced it with a necessary isomorphism invariant, five color-refinement rounds. All forbidden-word orbits under reversal/complement, 3 <= length < d, were screened through dimension 11 with no cross-nu invariant collision. Attempted dimension 12 hit wall cap; no complete dimension-12 coverage from that run. A separate vectorized canonical color-refinement implementation COMPLETED dimensions 4..12 with no cross-index collisions; dimension 12 covered 1083 reversal/complement orbit representatives. This supersedes only the coverage limit, not the killed-run receipts.','Need either a genuine counterexample in the nondegenerate source range or a theorem recovering nu from the induced graph in all dimensions. When |f|=d every graph is a cube minus one vertex, producing a routine formulation defect; this is explicitly excluded from credit.','1402.6377, nu definition at start Section 3, Theorem 3.1, Conjecture 3.2, Appendix A range(3,d)',('logs/cubes-r2.log','logs/cubes-invariant.log','logs/cubes12.log','logs/cubes-numpy.log'))
