add(334189,'parked_sustained_bounded_nonfinding','primary 2-increasing definition, decomposition mechanism and Conjectures 6.1-6.2 read; exact and heuristic searches','Every earlier triple must be strictly smaller in at least TWO coordinates than every later triple; consecutive comparisons are insufficient. Equality case requires a nontrivial Cartesian decomposition for at least one label coordinate.','Exact DFS on [n]^3 for n=2..5 found maxima 2,4,8,10. Additional rectangular exhaustive sweeps and all reached equality sequences used source rectangular-hull merging for decomposability. Complete [4]^3 sweep checked 12 equality sequences, all decomposable; six-by-six-by-six prefix search found length 14 but did not complete. Mutation searches at n=4,9,16 ran 229955, 21342, and 9999 trials respectively. Best lengths remained 8,27,64; 48010,728,23 equality-or-better sequences passed the decomposition diagnostic. Finite diagnostics receive zero theorem credit.','No obstruction to the global square-root bound and no indecomposable extremal sequence. Need a uniform proof exploiting extremality, or a verified finite witness; none exists in this packet.','1609.08688, initial 2-increasing definition, Section 6 pp.49-52, Conjecture 6.1',('logs/sequences.log','logs/sequence-deep.log','logs/sequence-mutate.log'))
add(335843,'excluded_known_full_scope_proof','original exact Conjecture 4.5 and all three successor construction/proof bodies read','Infinite locally finite counterexamples to Theorem 4.4(c), (e), and first part of (f): VT+NTC not SIS; D3-C+D3MF not both VT/FT; D3-C+D3MD not NCC.','Farley, Mathematica Pannonica 2022, DOI 10.1556/314.2022.00009, proves exactly these three claims. Proposition 3.1 gives two intertwined infinite chains; Propositions 4.2 and 5.2 use finite completion extensions and their increasing unions. Author-uploaded primary full text was read after DOI tool access failed.','No new result. Publisher DOI was inaccessible via web tool; no retry. Author-uploaded article text, including proof bodies and bibliographic dates, is preserved as tool receipts.','Farley 2022, Propositions 3.1, 4.2 and 5.2; Lemmas 4.1 and 5.1',extra=('receipts/poset-doi.json','receipts/poset-author-body.json','receipts/poset-author-body-tail.json','receipts/poset-author-body-end.json'))
